<title>USA: Georgia jobless rate edges up to 4.1 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Georgia jobless rate edges up to 4.1 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's unemployment rate edged up to 4.1 percent in May from 4 percent in April, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said Thursday.</p>
<p>That was down from 4.2 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Employment rates for May and April for Georgia's major urban areas were:</p>
<p>--Albany, 5.9 percent, up from 5.5 percnt.</p>
<p>--Athens, 2.5 perent, up from 2.4 percent.</p>
<p>--Atlanta, 3.4 percent, up from 3.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Augusta, 5.5 percent, up from 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Columbus, 4.4 percent, up from 4.1 percent.</p>
<p>--Macon, 4.3 percent, up from 4.2 percent.</p>
<p>--Savannah, 4.4 percent, up from 4.3 percent.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
